From: christianKEL <christian@e5m-ck>
Date: 2026-05-27
Subject: [PATCH] steppersync: serialize step generation per-steppersync

Empirical workaround for the recurring

    stepcompress o=<oid> i=<negative> c=1 a=0: Invalid sequence
    Error in syncemitter '<stepper_y>' step generation
    Internal error in stepcompress

shutdown reproduced on Klipper master bd09e017 (Crash 1, t~55000s) and
again on master 4bc56464 (Crash 2, t~31249s) on an Ender 5 Max +
Creality Nebula Pad printing OrcaSlicer gcode that carries ~50000
SET_VELOCITY_LIMIT SQUARE_CORNER_VELOCITY=... toggles.

steppersyncmgr_gen_steps() normally fans out itersolve_generate_steps()
to one background pthread per syncemitter and only joins at the end.
For coreXY the X/Y syncemitters share the same trapq. A straight reading
of itersolve_generate_steps() shows it only writes per-stepper state
(struct stepper_kinematics, struct stepcompress) while reading the
shared trapq, so a hard race is not obvious. But the bug is strongly
timing-sensitive (8-15h to fire, always on stepper_y on this coreXY
machine) and PR #7271's send-queue dump shows direction reversals at
very low speed (interval > 400000, count=1) immediately before the
failure -- exactly where any subtle inter-thread ordering between
sibling iterative solvers would matter.

This patch keeps the threading infrastructure intact but collapses the
start-all / finalize-all phases into a single per-syncemitter loop:
each syncemitter is signaled, joined, and only the next one is signaled
after. Background threads still exist but at most one runs at a time
within a given steppersync. CoreXY siblings can no longer overlap. If
the crash stops reproducing under this patch we have isolated it to
that overlap.

Applies cleanly on top of Klipper master 4bc5646.

---
 klippy/chelper/steppersync.c | 16 ++++++----------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/klippy/chelper/steppersync.c b/klippy/chelper/steppersync.c
--- a/klippy/chelper/steppersync.c
+++ b/klippy/chelper/steppersync.c
@@ -409,27 +409,23 @@ steppersyncmgr_gen_steps(struct steppersyncmgr *ssm, double flush_time
                 trapq_check_sentinels(tq);
         }
     }
-    // Start step generation threads
+    // E5M-CK patch: serialize gen_steps per syncemitter so that sibling
+    // steppers sharing a trapq (e.g. coreXY X/Y) never run
+    // itersolve_generate_steps() concurrently. See
+    // klipper/patches/0001-steppersync-serialize-gen-steps-per-steppersync.patch
+    struct syncemitter *failed_se = NULL;
     list_for_each_entry(ss, &ssm->ss_list, ssm_node) {
         uint64_t flush_clock = clock_from_time(&ss->ce, flush_time);
         uint64_t clear_clock = clock_from_time(&ss->ce, clear_history_time);
         struct syncemitter *se;
         list_for_each_entry(se, &ss->se_list, ss_node) {
             se_start_gen_steps(se, gen_steps_time, flush_clock, clear_clock);
-        }
-    }
-    // Wait for step generation threads to complete
-    struct syncemitter *failed_se = NULL;
-    list_for_each_entry(ss, &ssm->ss_list, ssm_node) {
-        struct syncemitter *se;
-        list_for_each_entry(se, &ss->se_list, ss_node) {
             int32_t ret = se_finalize_gen_steps(se);
             if (ret)
                 failed_se = se;
         }
         if (failed_se)
             continue;
-        uint64_t flush_clock = clock_from_time(&ss->ce, flush_time);
         steppersync_flush(ss, flush_clock);
     }
     return failed_se;
